Use zenity for the native file/folder pickers off Windows.

Upstream implements "Add folder" / "Add files" by writing a PowerShell script to
a temp file and spawning powershell to run it, guarded by a hard win32 check
that 501s everywhere else. The message it returns ("type the path instead")
points at a text input the viewer does not have, so on Linux there is no way to
import anything from the UI at all -- only `vault scan` from the CLI.

zenity prints exactly what the PowerShell shim printed, on the same stream: one
path for a folder, newline-separated paths for a multi-select. So both endpoints
(/api/import/pick-folder, /api/import/pick-files) and their parsing are left
untouched; only the process being spawned changes.

